[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186080003 :answer-field/choices 17592186080004] [:db/retract 17592186080003 :answer-field/choices 17592186080005] [:db/retract 17592186080003 :answer-field/choices 17592186080006] [:db/retract 17592186080003 :answer-field/choices 17592186080007] [:db/retract 17592186080003 :answer-field/choices 17592186080008] {:db/id 17592186083337 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" "question-f16d560c-09a5-5adf-953f-3ef2b521c424" "question-abc49f5c-860a-5246-8fd2-ba05f76f3a6e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083139 :question/worked-solution "![](images/b9/b970e539af5b695644486ad4eb7c21558c334ffd33c1df1a2343fac493d84389.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, we have a *negative* correlation.\n\n- The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, we have a *weak* correlation.\n\nTherefore, the variables have a *weak negative* linear correlation." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083338 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-09efb2e6-1e80-53f4-bf82-55db52baf7d8" "question-2e20c6e9-8a1f-5520-84a5-13e0b1715760" "question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" "question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083140 :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e3c58da0dc7f326497d9a7c1327d6d40f98684089694f9de88f21a64f4b4824.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the correlation coefficient for the data in the scatter plot above?\n\nI. $\\rho =-0.8$\n\nII. $\\rho= 0.3$\n\nIII. $\\rho = 0.9$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho$ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/06/06dcc617bbbc07fea756f35975146a238bd4cb9c4ce437f1b9300a7c05ded7b6.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *positive* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *positive*. Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho = -0.8\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho = 0.3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient from the given options is $\\rho= 0.9.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083339 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fdb0f84a-e85a-559c-9fae-e9b6176fb94c" "question-bc9c7169-1131-5a87-93ac-6b79642c5534" "question-06e32974-1b71-50c8-93f5-929432644d25" "question-d339220f-f17c-55cf-8865-ba521fdebae7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083141 :question/problem "It is known that there is a linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho\\approx -0.85,$ sketch a possible scatter plot that corresponds to this situation." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho$ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho \\approx -0.85,$ there is a *strong negative* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *negative* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *negative* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should lie *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation could correspond to the following scatter plot:\n\n![](images/ad/ad8ff5e49649b5e788b83eb28fa26afae61072d5e63026631a9cd1891be14a0c.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/id #uuid "e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134103" :question/problem "![](images/04/04fbb73cfa465f4cb052f3347a8651bae48140441c4fbfa753d2bd86ac41dfe8.png)\n\nA group of students is interviewed. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the hours they spent playing video games daily the week before the literature exam and the grade they got on the exam. Which of the following best describes the correlation between the variables in the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/91/91d928d021c8715a24fdb7dc262bec53c30626d8649a2ac451c94f9c0ecc0db0.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, we have a *negative* correlation.\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, we have a *strong* correlation.\n\nTherefore, the variables have a *strong negative* linear correlation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" "answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" "answer-8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8" "answer-29391afd-e40c-555e-af97-50ca4ab507f6" "answer-7184b1f4-449d-5810-934f-45a18f1048e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/id #uuid "da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "no linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer/id #uuid "548cb0fc-8599-5d