ld/correct 17592186079992 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-abc49f5c-860a-5246-8fd2-ba05f76f3a6e" :question/id #uuid "abc49f5c-860a-5246-8fd2-ba05f76f3a6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134099" :question/problem "![](images/25/2561ac832231961f439731ff16a5b918787b848fc41f77fb63e987c79d50f40b.png)\n\nA study is made on the grades of a group of high school students. The scatter plot above shows the relationship between grades obtained in the subjects of chemistry and mathematics. Which of the following best describes the correlation between the variables in the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "From the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02e3d693-e281-56a8-a4da-4749c2f3df92"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02e3d693-e281-56a8-a4da-4749c2f3df92" :answer-field/id #uuid "02e3d693-e281-56a8-a4da-4749c2f3df92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e934472d-0a94-531d-bdcd-4001307fafc7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e934472d-0a94-531d-bdcd-4001307fafc7" "answer-349057ee-b77b-5a2f-a3a1-1255acb11c2e" "answer-04c24679-f692-5bfb-9d7c-05f5dc96b029" "answer-69fd680b-f8f6-5f46-bd13-cd6083c3e0aa" "answer-45060158-a98c-561c-80cb-006ceb1d17b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e934472d-0a94-531d-bdcd-4001307fafc7" :answer/id #uuid "e934472d-0a94-531d-bdcd-4001307fafc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "no linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-349057ee-b77b-5a2f-a3a1-1255acb11c2e" :answer/id #uuid "349057ee-b77b-5a2f-a3a1-1255acb11c2e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "strong negative linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04c24679-f692-5bfb-9d7c-05f5dc96b029" :answer/id #uuid "04c24679-f692-5bfb-9d7c-05f5dc96b029" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "strong positive linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69fd680b-f8f6-5f46-bd13-cd6083c3e0aa" :answer/id #uuid "69fd680b-f8f6-5f46-bd13-cd6083c3e0aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "weak negative linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45060158-a98c-561c-80cb-006ceb1d17b5" :answer/id #uuid "45060158-a98c-561c-80cb-006ceb1d17b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "weak positive linear correlation" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083517 :question/worked-solution "From the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186079997 :answer-field/correct 17592186079998 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083518 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/91/91d605a297f2fd3c90c59592cc08184c4201f04ebc69bfc285e4261af8e918d2.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *negative*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.9,\\,\\rho ≈0.1,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $-1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈-0.8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186080003 :answer-field/correct "answer-cb7ee60a-05da-569e-8c17-f1335eac64cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5909bb2-0a90-52d9-b686-d0e61412bfbe" "answer-cb7ee60a-05da-569e-8c17-f1335eac64cb" "answer-0c7cb220-5afc-5b19-a7bf-aeaaba188e81" "answer-bf05904c-18b3-52af-a5c3-6e120a983a80" "answer-2ecf7776-f06c-5178-9d27-b89b7e8cfb8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5909bb2-0a90-52d9-b686-d0e61412bfbe" :answer/id #uuid "f5909bb2-0a90-52d9-b686-d0e61412bfbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb7ee60a-05da-569e-8c17-f1335eac64cb" :answer/id #uuid "cb7ee60a-05da-569e-8c17-f1335eac64cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c7cb220-5afc-5b19-a7bf-aeaaba188e81" :answer/id #uuid "0c7cb220-5afc-5b19-a7bf-aeaaba188e81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf05904c-18b3-52af-a5c3-6e120a983a80" :answer/id #uuid "bf05904c-18b3-52af-a5c3-6e120a983a80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ecf7776-f06c-5178-9d27-b89b7e8cfb8a" :answer/id #uuid "2ecf7776-f06c-5178-9d27-b89b7e8cfb8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-09efb2e6-1e80-53f4-bf82-55db52baf7d8" :question/id #uuid "09efb2e6-1e80-53f4-bf82-55db52baf7d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134122" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2f569fe07310e8bd068cda0152b296d7b1189efec03720a0d3a043a7ab52d21.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the age of some people and the average number of cups of coffee they consume daily. \nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nFrom the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation.\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4fae3beb-3510-5939-afed-b54d6ee4d3a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4fae3beb-3510-5939-afed-b54d6ee4d3a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4fae3beb-3510-5939-afed-b54d6ee4d3a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ef364a3-b3b6-5068-ab53-fbf996e0a6aa" "answer-ad977d26-9351-54cd-9449-7de02c055b6a" "answer-e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" "answer-01a7c6d4-0487-53da-a22e-734216f21437" "answer-9c99d273-eee7-551e-991e-7d2f5b565510"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ef364a3-b3b6-5068-ab53-fbf996e0a6aa" :answer/id #uuid "7ef364a3-b3b6-5068-ab53-fbf996e0a6aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad977d26-9351-54cd-9449-7de02c055b6a" :answer/id #uuid "ad977d26-9351-54cd-9449-7de02c055b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" :answer/id #uuid "e97f983b-8d60-5aec-9580-1d14d322c307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01a7c6d4-0487-53da-a22e-734216f21437" :answer/id #uuid "01a7c6d4-0487-53da-a22e-734216f21437" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c99d273-eee7-551e-991e-7d2f5b565510" :answer/id #uuid "9c99d273-eee7-551e-991e-7d2f5b565510" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2e20c6e9-8a1f-5520-84a5-13e0b1715760" :question/id #uuid "2e20c6e9-8a1f-5520-84a5-13e0b1715760" :question/math-academy-id "q-134126" :question/problem "![](images/27/271e5f80ff6ab311bcdbc6b2725516b16a5c3fee63b6d219a59801c78d4f77e4.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of shirts and the number of pants sold in a store over a certain number of days. \nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nFrom the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation.\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-157cc70f-8bfd-56d9-b601-f1ea6f2f9206"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-157cc70f-8bfd-56d9-b601-f1ea6f2f9206" :answer-field/id #uuid "157cc70f-8bfd-56d9-b601-f1ea6f2f9206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e340584d-ae6e-5e84-a152-3f6a2121b262" "answer-b3b980a5-1b07-53a0-bd99-f5969d3971f0" "answer-975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" "answer-647e1d76-8699-5f00-b950-f65a5d9a1e25" "answer-5fb66c80-1747-5cd6-b473-d39c5d64cf56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e340584d-ae6e-5e84-a152-3f6a2121b262" :answer/id #uuid "e340584d-ae6e-5e84-a152-3f6a2121b262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3b980a5-1b07-53a0-bd99-f5969d3971f0" :answer/id #uuid "b3b980a5-1b07-53a0-bd99-f5969d3971f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" :answer/id #uuid "975ac0a8-2d8e-501d-aae1-278a3552d5f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-647e1d76-8699-5f00-b950-f65a5d9a1e25" :answer/id #uuid "647e1d76-8699-5f00-b950-f65a5d9a1e25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fb66c80-1747-5cd6-b473-d39c5d64cf56" :answer/id #uuid "5fb66c80-1747-5cd6-b473-d39c5d64cf56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/id #uuid "9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/math-academy-id "q-134125" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c03191b325ee430f02216f35998db128ea99c6096222d489fa817f680e98d10.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time some college students spend studying at night for their final exams and the number of hours they sleep per night. Which of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/74/74aa691e42eea766595eede7d42d59e164509d6dbf3c8a609dd42e1196d11512.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *negative*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.8,\\,\\rho ≈0.4,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $0.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈-0.3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" "answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" "answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" "answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" "answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/id #uuid "fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/id #uuid "4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/id #uuid "f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/id #uuid "18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/id #uuid "52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/id #uuid "e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/math-academy-id "q-134120" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dd43d8833be95bd8b13a98b65dddd1272501599b107053296302cb7fae7e58b.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient for the data in the scatter plot above?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/ae/aecc569c03ed874748993b77ed09a8a318dae23bcaea09334d98af9da36d8a87.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *positive* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *positive*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.75,\\,\\rho ≈-0.3,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.85.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e71cb635-681e-51e0-8351-d1cc6f433ab1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-edd640cf-5862-5d11-9954-da14ddb5d70f" "answer-ffb7ea0c-c555-50e6-b6f4-54644915ff89" "answer-2042dc18-49bf-58fb-8c04-7b065a71ba6d" "answer-a0758947-9149-585c-80e7-966a2a53f237" "answer-e71cb635-681e-51e0-8351-d1cc6f433ab1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-edd640cf-5862-5d11-9954-da14ddb5d70f" :answer/id #uuid "edd640cf-5862-5d11-9954-da14ddb5d70f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\rho ≈