his situation?" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given situation.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should be scattered *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/f9/f918c0b1ec7a3b3969fef43eb60bba0b4d4afba813082d710c456d4c53a49018.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4725b4aa-c910-53da-8450-5672f21c1dcd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4725b4aa-c910-53da-8450-5672f21c1dcd" :answer-field/id #uuid "4725b4aa-c910-53da-8450-5672f21c1dcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-03b5013b-1b8d-5ea5-acf9-9e6a17e86485" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d550fa08-807e-5582-8d13-f5a808bd5ab5" "answer-213a7457-0aa0-5582-9c30-27c246a0e264" "answer-03b5013b-1b8d-5ea5-acf9-9e6a17e86485" "answer-c5f70bb9-2022-5afa-8862-75382ec4e6bb" "answer-203b2536-d575-5f4e-a892-d7791d774b7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d550fa08-807e-5582-8d13-f5a808bd5ab5" :answer/id #uuid "d550fa08-807e-5582-8d13-f5a808bd5ab5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1e/1ef3eba0a815bee2bbe1611ea0330e31c366b758e8306b247701a0a99fc22f20.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-213a7457-0aa0-5582-9c30-27c246a0e264" :answer/id #uuid "213a7457-0aa0-5582-9c30-27c246a0e264" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/21/2149ef0c7a9e2acd912081fce8b3a53a57f0d17edcb80842f491f1d0b10eb3e9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03b5013b-1b8d-5ea5-acf9-9e6a17e86485" :answer/id #uuid "03b5013b-1b8d-5ea5-acf9-9e6a17e86485" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/88/8878fd97d3c1ebb87b849bfb1da28b03821dc1f11fecf26fb98386fcbf8e1d83.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5f70bb9-2022-5afa-8862-75382ec4e6bb" :answer/id #uuid "c5f70bb9-2022-5afa-8862-75382ec4e6bb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ba/ba6cc98881a906e2da63d80a971714dcf8c3bf8f425818136624079f8394a981.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-203b2536-d575-5f4e-a892-d7791d774b7c" :answer/id #uuid "203b2536-d575-5f4e-a892-d7791d774b7c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/dc/dc4334cff1d792272fe5fe51b5b3973dd11388d46c5e3960361586b9d5602137.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-06e32974-1b71-50c8-93f5-929432644d25" :question/id #uuid "06e32974-1b71-50c8-93f5-929432644d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-134089" :question/problem "It's known that there is a weak positive linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given situation.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *weak*, most of the points should be scattered *far* from the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/8c/8c21367686723d7ce1165ec24f569658d77376a39d7962b8a4ed90b06c9e1220.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9528ef67-4f45-5de3-aca0-210693a78fb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9528ef67-4f45-5de3-aca0-210693a78fb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "9528ef67-4f45-5de3-aca0-210693a78fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e00c6bf5-0f55-5f97-8579-b3ea77041d54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff8e3165-ed64-5f28-8f2e-1b00d3e8d8c7" "answer-5945c633-8bc2-5ee0-bc53-00f8c762ef88" "answer-e6601fe7-4e9c-5edd-b66e-c2e245ea68b7" "answer-b7c515da-0b10-5b3f-b4bb-59a9caefaf0f" "answer-e00c6bf5-0f55-5f97-8579-b3ea77041d54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff8e3165-ed64-5f28-8f2e-1b00d3e8d8c7" :answer/id #uuid "ff8e3165-ed64-5f28-8f2e-1b00d3e8d8c7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/3a/3ad7850563975ed74e5eaac3ea887bfdb3c93422df7c6f30f9eb77509ece333a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5945c633-8bc2-5ee0-bc53-00f8c762ef88" :answer/id #uuid "5945c633-8bc2-5ee0-bc53-00f8c762ef88" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/67/676dd6bfce76b7f3743338c7a5c74bdd6b19e6dcc06bb7ae507099e026fed498.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6601fe7-4e9c-5edd-b66e-c2e245ea68b7" :answer/id #uuid "e6601fe7-4e9c-5edd-b66e-c2e245ea68b7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/8f/8fbe10c5f9013a3ceb408aec32b986bedac02011960845182f20b4a98bc4e4b9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7c515da-0b10-5b3f-b4bb-59a9caefaf0f" :answer/id #uuid "b7c515da-0b10-5b3f-b4bb-59a9caefaf0f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ad/adad3f224d705f4341928547dd0971f9ac9b8fc0705cea3d0e72de2da1ecadb6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e00c6bf5-0f55-5f97-8579-b3ea77041d54" :answer/id #uuid "e00c6bf5-0f55-5f97-8579-b3ea77041d54" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec0784db5054c47cfa60ed437b21e836fd39e9e1a64fa5227430249a3b05a749.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d339220f-f17c-55cf-8865-ba521fdebae7" :question/id #uuid "d339220f-f17c-55cf-8865-ba521fdebae7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134112" :question/problem "It's known that there is a linear correlation between the height (in $\\text{cm}$) and weight (in $\\text{kg}$) of a group of students in a particular class. Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho ≈0.45,$ which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho ≈0.45,$ there is a *weak positive* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *weak*, most of the points should be scattered *far* from the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/31/31aef47ad76d8cd4c7e967ccc7b8ca523eb3a20af440454bc7908bbe9441c918.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" "answer-8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" "answer-26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" "answer-1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" :answer/id #uuid "be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/10/10408bda83013b4decbf51370d20018004a1086a538322abbd0b9da1b910e4f2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" :answer/id #uuid "8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/14/14258fd15361beae5d6e0655e81051b2e4bfd95d20b05dc98113558e43412f41.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" :answer/id #uuid "26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a8/a866fcee0e975c0741299a5e1504470dbae44e18b541149c7d5e1e2acb9b32bd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" :answer/id #uuid "1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec4b106cf763a4c54ee2b1d8eecf6e7b91e371b0dd38198502bd433ef7e6e371.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/id #uuid "9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec7a1b76ebbcc4965824be26bc4b1e630167b032855498df6d492a61461fecf9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083521 :question/problem "It is known that there is a linear correlation between the number of years passed since $2000$ and the population of a particular town. Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho ≈0.9,$ which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho ≈0.9,$ there is a *strong positive* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should lie *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/aa/aac79b793bde599899ff7ff8ca880e198bd5481178c2c5a0e2ac96acf223bdaa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186080021 :answer-field/correct 17592186080025 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084452 :tutorial/content "There is a **linear correlation** between two sets of paired observations if the data points on the corresponding scatter plot are located along a straight line.\n\nWe say that the correlation is **positive** if the corresponding trend line has a *positive slope*. Similarly, we say that the correlation is **negative** if the corresponding trend line has a *negative slope*.\n\nWe have a **strong** correlation if the data points lie *close* to the corresponding trend line. Similarly, we have a **weak** correlation if the data points are scattered *far* from the corresponding trend line.\n\nLet's see a few examples:\n\n| ![](images/cd/cdd335fda9e91cbf7cdb05ad18065630985c50adb788df980708d822f7a5e8e9.png) | **Strong positive** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | **Weak positive** linear correlation: \n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | **Strong negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| ![](images/07/076440b257a78474e9f1b3129ec448a407bb1b49215a29251d8e929cadaeb984.png) | **Weak negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/ed/ed266d09a86d7200c02f004cd9bb3a87f75693462ff8846f7f3cc1ed4b66ed63.png) | **No linear correlation**:\n\n- The data points are scattered randomly. |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084490 :tutorial/content "The linear **correlation coefficient** $\\rho$ (the Greek letter rho, pronounced \"row\") is a real number between $-1$ and $1$ that shows the strength of a linear correlation. It has the following properties:\n\n- $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation\n\n- $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation\n\n- $\\rho = 0$ indicates no (linear) correlation\n\nThe approximate value of $\\rho$ can be determined from the scatter plot.\n\n| ![](images/09/09d585da995df4e5a67b022816eec246113171d3aad15dcb57d82c766dcb7d18.png) | For a strong positive correlation, we have $0.7 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1.$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | For a weak positive correlation, we have $0.3 \\leq \\rho \\lt 0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | For a strong negative correlation, we have $-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq -0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/92/92b65a115fd1621303a248de8ae03d05392827914f5200f267d368867d511ae5.png) | For a weak negative correlation, we have $-0.7 \\lt \\rho \\leq -0.3.$ |\n| ![](images/2c/2cf1e2c3e79940229fc85c10d5bccdfed17afe0759cc897d53e5421328b21466.png) | For little or no correlation, we have $-0.3 < \\rho < 0.3.$ |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083427 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186083139 :question/worked-solution "![](images/b9/b970e539af5b695644486ad4eb7c21558c334ffd33c1df1a2343fac493d84389.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, we have a *negative* correlation.\n\n- The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, we have a *weak* correlation.\n\nTherefore, the variables have a *weak negative* linear correlation."] [17592186083140 :question/problem "![](images/4e/4e3c58da0dc7f326497d9a7c1327d6d40f98684089694f9de88f21a64f4b4824.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the correlation coefficient for the data in the scatter plot above?\n\nI. $\\rho =-0.8$\n\nII. $\\rho= 0.3$\n\nIII. $\\rho = 0.9$"] [17592186083140 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho$ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/06/06dcc617bbbc07fea756f35975146a238bd4cb9c4ce437f1b9300a7c05ded7b6.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *positive* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *positive*. Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho = -0.8\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho = 0.3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient from the given options is $\\rho= 0.9.$"] [17592186083141 :question/problem "It is known that there is a linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho\\approx -0.85,$ sketch a possible scatter plot that corresponds to this situation."] [17592186083141 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho$ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho \\approx -0.85,$ there is a *strong negative* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *negative* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *negative* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should lie *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation could correspond to the following scatter plot:\n\n![](images/ad/ad8ff5e49649b5e788b83eb28fa26afae61072d5e63026631a9cd1891be14a0c.png)"] ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/id #uuid "e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7"] ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134103"] ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/problem "![](images/04/04fbb73cfa465f4cb052f3347a8651bae48140441c4fbfa753d2bd86ac41dfe8.png)\n\nA group of students is interviewed. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the hours they spent playing video games daily the week before the literature exam and the grade they got on the exam. Which of the following best describes the correlation between the variables in the scatter plot?"] ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/worked-solution "![](images/91/91d928d021c8715a24fdb7dc262bec53c30626d8649a2ac451c94f9c0ecc0db0.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, we have a *negative* correlation.\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, we have a *strong* correlation.\n\nTherefore, the variables have a *strong negative* linear correlation."] ["question-e2c56edd-8fb8-5a8e-abe8-142f14623ed7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2702c34-c7e9-5325-9741-8ce3622c97cd"] ["answer-da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/id #uuid "da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692"] ["answer-da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-da723436-8cde-5bcc-ab9f-5d1691728692" :answer/value "no linear correlation"] ["answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer/id #uuid "548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9"] ["answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-548cb0fc-8599-5d8e-a01c-66d33541fbb9" :answer/value "strong negative linear correlation"] ["answer-8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8" :answer/id #uuid "8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8"] ["answer-8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8231fe35-d847-50c6-b767-316e740854a8" :answer/value "strong positive linear correlation"] ["answer-29391af