t/questions "question-2e20c6e9-8a1f-5520-84a5-13e0b1715760"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/id #uuid "9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/math-academy-id "q-134125"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c03191b325ee430f02216f35998db128ea99c6096222d489fa817f680e98d10.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the time some college students spend studying at night for their final exams and the number of hours they sleep per night. Which of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/74/74aa691e42eea766595eede7d42d59e164509d6dbf3c8a609dd42e1196d11512.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *negative* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *negative*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.8,\\,\\rho ≈0.4,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $0.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈-0.3.$"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1"] ["answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/id #uuid "fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178"] ["answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178" :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.3"] ["answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/id #uuid "4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0"] ["answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0" :answer/value "\\rho ≈-0.9"] ["answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/id #uuid "f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70"] ["answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70" :answer/value "\\rho ≈0"] ["answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/id #uuid "18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e"] ["answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e" :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.4"] ["answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/id #uuid "52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81"] ["answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81" :answer/value "\\rho ≈0.8"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/correct "answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/choices "answer-fa53955d-d092-59ca-bedb-4ee2c6e6f178"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/choices "answer-4dde781b-7d3c-5e90-88e4-b6e543af6cd0"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/choices "answer-f4ea6508-51c1-5ee1-974c-71ab52286e70"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/choices "answer-18de5bcf-ee53-583d-9955-d6382d059b1e"] ["answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1" :answer-field/choices "answer-52f0bd21-8e5a-5e90-94c5-b78bb36bcb81"] ["question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f26454ee-b84b-57c9-bd6b-8ffaabec57a1"] [17592186083338 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9f7eb28b-e6d3-58a7-ad9a-3a6681ca1ee4"] ["question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/id #uuid "e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52"] ["question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/math-academy-id "q-134120"] ["question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dd43d8833be95bd8b13a98b65dddd1272501599b107053296302cb7fae7e58b.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient for the data in the scatter plot above?"] ["question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n![](images/ae/aecc569c03ed874748993b77ed09a8a318dae23bcaea09334d98af9da36d8a87.png)\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a *positive* slope. So, the correlation coefficient must be *positive*. Thus, we disregard the following values:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈-0.75,\\,\\rho ≈-0.3,\\,\\rho ≈0\n$$\n\n- The points lie pretty close to the corresponding trend line. So, the correlation coefficient must be closer to $1.$ Thus, we disregard the following value:\n\n$$\n\\rho ≈0.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.85.$"] ["question-e6c59cf1-e1f3-5c09-adfe-bd7d9e53be52" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "724bde99-b3bb-58df-81bd-552e8017bb6e"] ["answer-edd640cf